      "type": "text",
      "text": "I've flagged the run as anomalous, most likely because of an exhaust blockage (moderate confidence), and suggested pausing it.\n\n- **What's wrong:** Tube pressure has risen steadily during growth, from 3.05 Torr at t=2640 s to 3.49 Torr at t=3240 s. That's about 0.1 Torr every two minutes. Through the ramp it held flat at about 3.04 Torr.\n- **Why an exhaust blockage:** Argon flow held at about 100 sccm, so more gas coming in doesn't explain it. Exhaust oxygen stayed at 4–6 ppm, so air isn't getting in, which argues against a seal leak. Temperature (750 °C) and heater power look normal.\n- **Not confirmed yet:** I have no pump or throttle valve readings and no normal-run reference range for pressure. Checking the pump-side pressure or valve position would confirm or rule out the blockage.\n- **Growth result:** The sample hasn't been characterized, so there's no evidence either way on whether the material grew."
     }
